<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- arcfox: values-sw430dp is a COVER-DISPLAY-ONLY qualifier on this device. The
     cover panel is 1080x1272 at 360 dpi = 480x565 dp (smallest width 480), the inner
     panel is 1080x2640 at 420 dpi = 411x1005 dp (smallest width 411 < 430). Measured
     with `wm density` / `dumpsys display` on 2026-09-13.

     The cover's rear camera block covers x 585..1080, y 923..1272 px. The block is
     NOT declared as a display cutout (see the framework overlay: on AOSP a bottom
     cutout kills scrolling in the whole bottom strip), so the two things that would
     otherwise land under the cameras are moved here instead:
       - the hotseat gets extra bottom space so the dock icons end above y=923
         (they were centred at y~1100, 135 px tall)
       - the IME window alone is told the navigation bar is taller, so the keyboard's
         bottom row (ended at y=1130 with a 54 px bar) ends above y=923 (measured
         y~910). Portrait only: Launcher3 applies it for ROTATION_0 with the bar at
         the bottom; in landscape the block is at a side, not under the key rows.
     px/dp on the cover = 2.25.

     Sizes follow stock's own restriction, not the glass: Motorola's framework keeps
     app windows 297 px (config_cli_display_cutout_camera_height) above the bottom
     edge, letting content run 52 px into the rounded top of the block (measured
     from the decompiled W1UXS36H services.jar). Dock icons therefore end at y~947
     and the keyboard's bottom row at y~961 (block glass starts at y=923).

     Landscape: stock cuts a 297 px strip on the camera side for every app. Here
     taskbar_covered_side_inset_landscape makes Launcher3's taskbar provide a second
     navigationBars inset on that side in rotations 90/270, so app bounds, window
     frames and the keyboard lay out around it like a side navigation bar; portrait
     keeps the whole panel.

     History: the override was briefly blamed for the inner panel staying black
     after unfolding. That was a separate defect (the device-state table lacked
     PROPERTY_POWER_CONFIGURATION_TRIGGER_WAKE, so a long fold did not wake on
     open; see fold/device_state_configuration.xml). Its one real fault, a launcher
     crash when the override SET changed between panels, is fixed in the Launcher3
     patch by keeping the entry constant. -->
<resources>
    <dimen name="hotseat_bar_bottom_space_extra">97dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="taskbar_ime_bottom_inset_override">123dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="taskbar_covered_side_inset_landscape">297px</dimen>
</resources>
